[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585043499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3585043499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3585043499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vr2wr","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T10:03:40Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T10:06:04Z","body":"> This PR attempts to preserve the behavior of pre-existing projects by explicitly setting the driver to `vulkan` if it was unconfigured (default) prior to upgrading to 4.6. (Uses the approach added by @KoBeWi in #112607.) \r\n\r\nI changed the implementation to use @Calinou's approach in #105737 instead used for making Jolt Physics the default 3D physics engine only on newly created projects.\r\n\r\nSo this is now the same for D3D12, projects created in 4.6 will set `rendering/rendering_device/driver.windows` to `d3d12` automatically, but the default stays `vulkan` for compatibility. This affects projects created either via the Project Manager or `touch project.godot`, as there's logic applying these changes to empty `project.godot` files.\r\n\r\nThis is a conservative approach that lets people use D3D12 by default on new projects but without risk of breaking projects in production. An advantage of this approach is that for users who select D3D12 explicitly in 4.6, and then switch back and forth between 4.5 and 4.6 for any reason, the setting will be preserved. With the former approach where the default value changed, the setting would be lost when it matches the engine version's default.\r\n\r\nWe could consider going further in 4.7 and fully changing the default to D3D12 without further compatibility code, so all projects would be upgraded by then (and could still select back Vulkan after upgrade).\r\n\r\nWe should document this well, both in the release page and in the online docs, so users understand that while their pre-existing projects aren't automatically updated, we strongly recommend that they switch to using D3D12 in production from 4.6.\r\n\r\nWe could consider having some sort of post-upgrade dialog that gives users some options on how to deal with compatibility changes:\r\n- Switch to Jolt Physics\r\n- Switch to D3D 12\r\n- Run the MeshInstance3D upgrade tool for skeleton paths\r\n- etc.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585043499/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586857572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3586857572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3586857572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vyxpk","user":{"login":"lord-muad-dib","id":185235730,"node_id":"U_kgDOCwp5Eg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185235730?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib","html_url":"https://github.com/lord-muad-dib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T17:22:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T17:22:26Z","body":"on my configuration the d3d12 rd doesn't work well, the editor especially is very slow and it also affects every other app i'm running alongside godot, while on vulkan i don't see slowdowns. similar issues using either the igpu (intel u630) or the dgpu (nvidia 1050ti).\r\ni hope the development of the vulkan rd for windows doesn't stop after this.\r\njust my two cents, thanks","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586857572/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586955600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3586955600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3586955600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VzJlQ","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T18:08:06Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T18:08:23Z","body":"> i hope the development of the vulkan rd for windows doesn't stop after this. just my two cents, thanks\r\n\r\nGodot uses the same Vulkan RD for all platforms, there's no Windows-specific implementation. It can't really stop development.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586955600/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587101036","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3587101036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3587101036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VztFs","user":{"login":"lord-muad-dib","id":185235730,"node_id":"U_kgDOCwp5Eg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185235730?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib","html_url":"https://github.com/lord-muad-dib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T19:27:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T19:30:03Z","body":"> > i hope the development of the vulkan rd for windows doesn't stop after this. just my two cents, thanks\r\n> \r\n> Godot uses the same Vulkan RD for all platforms, there's no Windows-specific implementation. It can't really stop development.\r\n\r\nyes i understand that, my remark is in context of this pr.. i mean, the team is willing to switch defaults because there are few kinks not working perfectly on windows yet. fine i guess (i might not think this is ready Yet, hence my comment, but i'm not The Community, so). i hope there's still will to keep vulkan on windows getting better, that's it,\r\nbest of luck on your work on the d3d12 rd, Dario and bluesky,\r\nthanks","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587101036/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587235576","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3587235576","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3587235576,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V0N74","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T20:46:29Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T20:46:29Z","body":">  the team is willing to switch defaults because there are few kinks not working perfectly on windows ye\r\n\r\nThe Vulkan backend works great and is our most polished graphics API backend. The problem we are solving here is the fact that every couple of months AMD and NVidia ship broken Vulkan drivers that break every single Godot game. We can't improve the quality of the drivers shipped by AMD and NVidia, so our only option is to avoid Vulkan on Windows","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587235576/reactions","total_count":13,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":5,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3589373511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3589373511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3589373511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V8X5H","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T13:36:06Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T13:36:06Z","body":"> i hope the development of the vulkan rd for windows doesn't stop after this.\r\n\r\nFrom the [conversation here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103844#issuecomment-2708986080), it appears we are translating SPIRV to DXIL, which might explains the slower start-up time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3589373511/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3590840610","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3590840610","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3590840610,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WB-Ei","user":{"login":"TheAenema","id":94260384,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZ5MoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94260384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema","html_url":"https://github.com/TheAenema","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheAenema/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-29T01:55:51Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T01:55:51Z","body":"I'm working on my engine which is based on Godot and I'm porting the entire render and shader pipeline to D3D12 and HLSL. While moving fully to D3D12 I encountered the same startup performance issue.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, even with the changes [@blueskythlikesclouds](https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds) made, there is still a slowdown at startup. I spent the last two days tracking down the cause and here’s what I found:\r\n\r\nThe main reason for the slowdown is not the Godot renderer itself, but rather the core design of Godot by running multiple instances from the same executable.\r\n\r\n**Here's what's happening:**\r\n\r\n- It seems Direct3D 12 does not handle running multiple instances of the same `.exe` name well. Godot maintains its own shader cache on D3D12, but the Direct3D 12 runtime also uses its separate cache system.\r\n- When the game is launched for the first time, the Direct3D 12 runtime creates a shader cache with the system-wide UID `F4EB2D6C-ED2B-4BDD-AD9D-F913287E6768`. This entry appears under `C:\\Users\\<Username>\\AppData\\Local\\D3DSCache\\<App_Unique_Hash>` and the process takes about 5–10 seconds.\r\n- This `<App_Unique_Hash>` is generated as a hash of the executable name. I couldn’t find documentation on how this hash is produced, but it seems deterministic with respect to the `.exe` name. (Example: `godot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe` → `36d7303850b645a8`)\r\n- Now that the cache is created at `C:\\Users\\X\\AppData\\Local\\D3DSCache\\9a3e6cf38014fb9a\\F4EB2D6C-ED2B-4BDD-AD9D-F913287E6768.*` a second launch of the game starts much faster because it reuses the D3DSCache. However, if another instance of the engine is already running, whether editor or runtime, it also attempts to access the cache. Since the cache is locked by the first process, the new instance falls back to full shader compilation, which adds another 5–10 seconds to startup.\r\n\r\nIt doesn’t matter whether we're running the editor, debug mode or runtime first. When one instance is already active, a second instance cannot use the cache in D3DSCache because it is locked by the first process.\r\n\r\nI can think of two possible solutions at the moment:\r\n\r\n1. Install low-level hooks to virtualize engine access to the cache files. The flow would look like:  \r\n   `Engine <-> D3D <-> Virtualized Layer <-> Cache File`\r\n\r\n2. Compile the engine as a library (`libGodot.dll`) and provide two separate executables such as `Editor.exe` and `Runtime.exe` (by proxifying entrypoints). In this setup, the editor would launch the game using the `Runtime.exe` decoy instead of running it directly from itself.\r\n\r\nI'm not certain whether implementing `pipeline_cache_create` would resolve this issue, but it may be worth trying.\r\n```CPP\r\nbool RenderingDeviceDriverD3D12::pipeline_cache_create(const Vector<uint8_t> &p_data) {\r\n    WARN_PRINT(\"PSO caching is not implemented yet in the Direct3D 12 driver.\");\r\n    return false;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid RenderingDeviceDriverD3D12::pipeline_cache_free() {\r\n    ERR_FAIL_MSG(\"Not implemented.\");\r\n}\r\n\r\nsize_t RenderingDeviceDriverD3D12::pipeline_cache_query_size() {\r\n    ERR_FAIL_V_MSG(0, \"Not implemented.\");\r\n}\r\n\r\nVector<uint8_t> RenderingDeviceDriverD3D12::pipeline_cache_serialize() {\r\n    ERR_FAIL_V_MSG(Vector<uint8_t>(), \"Not implemented.\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nRelated issue: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103844\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3590840610/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":4},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3591657355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3591657355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3591657355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WFFeL","user":{"login":"lord-muad-dib","id":185235730,"node_id":"U_kgDOCwp5Eg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185235730?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib","html_url":"https://github.com/lord-muad-dib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lord-muad-dib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-29T12:58:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T12:58:55Z","body":"> > i hope the development of the vulkan rd for windows doesn't stop after this.\r\n> \r\n> From the [conversation here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103844#issuecomment-2708986080), it appears we are translating SPIRV to DXIL, which might explains the slower start-up time.\r\n\r\nif it was just the startup i wouldn't care much, actually....\r\n\r\nthe interface gets visibly slower, and it greatly affects other running apps aswell. alongside all the well known issues that are getting addressed.\r\n\r\nwith all due respects, d3d drivers of all manifacturers get regressions all the time, just like in vulkan is getting, and the godot community is just witnessing issues because vulkan was the de facto renderer everyone used so far...\r\n\r\nbut the choice has been made.. so..","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3591657355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3591724402","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113213#issuecomment-3591724402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113213","id":3591724402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WFV1y","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","su